TODO - Future Iterations
========================

  [ ] 1. Handle impl-before-class ordering
   - Currently: if an impl block appears before its class declaration in source code,
     SymTabCreationVisitor::visit(startNode&) reports "Missing Class Declaration"
     because the class hasn't been inserted into the global symbol table yet.
   - Fix: do a two-pass scan over startNode children:
       Pass 1: insert all classdecl entries into the global map
       Pass 2: process impldef entries (merging into already-registered classes)
   - This decouples source ordering from symbol resolution.
   - Location: visitor.cpp, SymTabCreationVisitor::visit(startNode&), ~line 148
  [ ] 2. Parameter types match declaration (in order): for each position,
         compare the impl param type to the decl param type.
         Note: param order matters; map lookup by name is not sufficient here —
         need to compare by position using an ordered list.


========================================================================
SEMANTIC CHECKS — planned for SemanticCheckingVisitor
========================================================================

Priority order — do in this sequence (later items depend on earlier ones):
  TIER 1 (foundation):  s, t
  TIER 2 (require s+t):  u, v, w, k(b), q
  TIER 3 (independent):  r, g, j, l, m, n

In visit(implNode&)    [implementation block checks]
------------------------------------------------------
  [x] a. Declared function exists: the function name being implemented
         must exist in the class's symbol table (classEntry->link).
  [x] b. Return type matches declaration: the returntype in the impl's
         funchead must equal the declared return type in the class.
  [x] c. Parameter count matches declaration: count params in impl's funchead
         against count in the corresponding class funcdecl entry's link map.
  [x] e. No duplicate implementations: the same class::function should not be
         implemented more than once. Track in a set<pair<className, funcName>>.

In visit(classNode&)   [class declaration checks]
--------------------------------------------------
  [ ] g. Inherited class exists: every id in the isalist must be found in the
         global symbol table as kind="class". Report error if not found.
         Access: iterate child with semanticMeaning=="isalist", check each id's nodeValue.
  [ ] h. No member name shadows inherited member (warning-level, optional).

In visit(startNode&)   [global-scope checks]
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [ ] i. Every declared class has at least one implementation block.
         (Already done in SymTabCreationVisitor — may want to move/duplicate here.)
  [ ] j. Exactly one main function exists and its return type is void.
  [ ] r. Circular class dependency: build a directed graph where edge A→B means
         class A has a data member of type B or inherits from B. Run DFS/Kahn's
         cycle detection. For each cycle report:
         "circular class dependency involving <classA> and <classB>".
         Run after symbol table is fully built.

In visit(funcNode&)    [free function / main checks]
-----------------------------------------------------
  [ ] k. Return type consistency:
         (a) if returntype != "void", verify a return statement exists.
         (b) The type of the return expression must equal the declared return type.
             Requires expression type inference (item s) to be done first.
  [ ] l. No duplicate free function names at global scope.

In visit(vardeclNode&)  [local variable declaration checks]
------------------------------------------------------------
  [ ] m. If variable type is a class name (e.g. "LOCAL f1: LINEAR"), verify
         that class exists in global symbol table.
  [ ] n. If a constructor call (aparams) is present on the vardecl, verify:
           - the class has a declared constructor
           - argument count matches constructor parameter count
           - argument types match constructor parameter types
         Access: vardecl → dimlist → aparams children for the arguments.

In visit(aparamsandidNode&)   [function call checks]
----------------------------------------------------
  [ ] o. Called function exists in the current scope or class scope.
         Error: "use of undeclared free function <name>" or
                "use of undeclared member function <name>" depending on context.
  [ ] p. Argument count matches the declared parameter count.
  [ ] q. Argument types match declared parameter types.
         Requires expression type inference (item s) to be done first.
         Array parameters: check compatible dimensionality (item w).

In type inference pass   [expression type resolution — req 10, 11]
------------------------------------------------------------------
  [ ] s. Expression type inference: annotate each expression node with its
         resolved type (bottom-up pass, new visitor or recursive helper):
           - intlit → "integer",  floatlit → "float",  stringlit → "string"
           - identifier → declared type from scope chain lookup
           - arithmetic (+,-,*,/): int op int → int; float op float → float;
             mixed → type error
           - relational (<,>,==,!=,<=,>=) → "integer" (boolean as int)
           - dot access → resolve via item v
           - function call → declared return type of the called function
         Store result on AST node (e.g. node.inferredType) for later visitors.
  [ ] t. Undeclared identifier checks (req 11): during the type inference walk,
         check every identifier against the active scope chain. Emit:
           "use of undeclared variable <name>"
           "use of undeclared free function <name>"
           "use of undeclared member function <name>"
           "use of undeclared class <name>"

In visit(assignNode&)   [assignment statement checks — req 10]
--------------------------------------------------------------
  [ ] u. Assignment type checking: resolve LHS and RHS types using item s.
         If types differ, emit:
         "type error in assignment: cannot assign <rhsType> to <lhsType>".

In visit(dotNode&)   ["." operator checks — req 15]
----------------------------------------------------
  [ ] v. Dot operator validation:
         (a) If LHS is not a class type, emit:
             "dot operator applied to non-class type <type>".
         (b) Look up RHS in the LHS class's symbol table.
             Data member missing: "undeclared data member <name> in class <className>".
             Member function missing: "undeclared member function <name> in class <className>".
         Requires item s for LHS type resolution.

In visit(arrayIndexNode&)   [array access checks — req 13]
----------------------------------------------------------
  [ ] w. Array dimension consistency:
         (a) Index count must equal declared dimensions; emit:
             "wrong number of dimensions for array <name>: expected <n>, got <m>".
         (b) Each index expression must be integer type; emit:
             "array index must be of integer type, got <type>".
         (c) Array passed as parameter must have compatible dimensionality; emit:
             "incompatible array dimensionality for parameter <name>".
         Requires items s and t.

